course: dictionary
lesson: 2128
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word coo is a good example. «A male pigeon puffs out his neck, coos and turns in circles» is about a bird making its soft, low sound.
explain: «Everyone who visits says, “Oh, the baby!” and coos at the cot» uses coo for a different action. Here it means speaking softly and lovingly, the way grown-ups talk to babies. The clue is the baby in the cot, not a bird.
explain: Ask who or what is doing the action. A pigeon, a dove, a baby or a grown-up can all coo, so the subject tells you a lot. Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Coo can be a verb, a noun or an interjection, and its job in the sentence changes its meaning.
fact: «Coo» as a verb means a pigeon or dove makes its soft, low, round sound.
fact: «Coo» as a verb can also mean to speak softly and lovingly, as people do to babies.
fact: «A coo» as a noun is the soft sound a dove makes, or a baby's happy sound.
fact: «Coo!» (UK, old-fashioned) is an exclamation of surprise, like «Wow!»
exercise: «A male pigeon puffs out his neck, coos and turns in circles to show off.» What does coos mean here? | Shakes its feathers dry | Runs away quickly | Flies very high into the sky | *Makes its soft, low sound
exercise: «Everyone who visits says, “Oh, the baby!” and coos at the cot.» What does coos mean here? | Sings a loud song | *Speaks softly and lovingly, the way you talk to a baby | Shouts loudly to wake everyone | Laughs at a funny joke
exercise: In an old-fashioned British story, someone sees a huge cake and says «Coo!» What does this show? | *Surprise | Sleepiness | Anger | Hunger for lunch
test: In «She heard a soft coo from the nest», what kind of word is coo? | Adjective | Interjection | Verb | *Noun
test: In «She cooed over her new puppy», what does cooed mean? | Barked loudly at | Ran away from | Ate quickly | *Spoke softly and lovingly to
exam: Which sentence uses coo to mean speak softly and lovingly? | *«She cooed over her new puppy.» | «The dove flew away over the hill.» | «The bird puffed out its neck.» | «The pigeon cooed on the roof.»
